{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Prerequisites","context":"## Set up IAM access\n\nYou must have the following IAM permissions in order to access your carbon emission data from AWS Sustainability.\n\n* `sustainability:GetEstimatedCarbonEmissions`\n* `sustainability:GetEstimatedCarbonEmissionsDimensionValues`\n\nYou must have the following IAM permissions in order to access water withdrawals data from AWS Sustainability.\n\n* `sustainability:GetEstimatedWaterAllocation`\n* `sustainability:GetEstimatedWaterAllocationDimensionValues`\n\nFor more information regarding IAM permissions, see Identity and access management for AWS Sustainability","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sustainability/latest/userguide/setting-up.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Integrate AWS carbon and water data into your ESG reporting | AWS Global Infrastructure and Sustainability Blog","context":"## 2. Native connectors in 3rd party tools\n\nYour ESG platform may offer a pre-built AWS connector that automatically imports AWS carbon and water data. The concrete steps depend on the tool you use. Typically, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Provide access, typically using one of the following:\n 1. an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) user\n 2. an IAM role that trusts the tool’s AWS account\n2. Grant least privileges, depending on the API used to access the data:\n 1. The IAM policy actions for the AWS Sustainability API are:\n\n```\n \"Action\": [\n \"sustainability:GetEstimatedCarbonEmissions\",\n \"sustainability:GetEstimatedCarbonEmissionsDimensionValues\",\n \"sustainability:GetEstimatedWaterAllocation\",\n \"sustainability:GetEstimatedWaterAllocationDimensionValues\"\n ]\n```\n\nb. To read Carbon emissions Data Exports on Amazon S3, the 3rd party tool requires at least read access to the objects in S3.\n\n 3. Configure the ESG reporting tool to automatically pull carbon and water data on a scheduled basis for dashboards, reports, and analytics.\n\nAn example of a native connector is the **Sweep sustainability intelligence platform**. It provides a native AWS connector that you can authorize and enable. Once configured, carbon emissions data flows automatically into Sweep, consolidated alongside other emission sources.\n\nIf your ESG reporting tool has a native connector for the AWS Sustainability API or Carbon Emissions Data Exports, that is the fastest path to automation. If it does not, or if you need more control over the data delivery, the following section walks you through building a custom solution","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/infrastructure-sustainability/integrate-aws-carbon-and-water-data-into-your-esg-reporting/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Identity-based policy examples for AWS Sustainability","context":"## Using the AWS Sustainability console\n\nTo access the AWS Sustainability console, you must have a minimum set of permissions.\nThese permissions must allow you to list and view details about the AWS Sustainability resources\nin your AWS account. If you create an identity-based policy that is more restrictive\nthan the minimum required permissions, the console won't function as intended for\nentities (users or roles) with that policy.\n\nYou don't need to allow minimum console permissions for users that are making calls\nonly to the AWS CLI or the AWS API. Instead, allow access to only the actions that match\nthe API operation that they're trying to perform.\n\nTo ensure that users and roles can still use the AWS Sustainability console, also attach the\nAWS Sustainability `ConsoleAccess` or `ReadOnly` AWS managed policy to\nthe entities. For more information, see Adding permissions to a user in the\n*IAM User Guide*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sustainability/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.html"}]}}

## Recent AWS announcements (What's New)

Newer than your training data may be. When these conflict with the documentation results above or with what you remember, prefer the most recent dated source.

{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Service Reference Information now supports SDK Operation to Action mapping - AWS","context":"AWS has updated its service reference information to include a mapping of operations supported by AWS services and the required IAM permissions to call those operations. This feature aims to help users determine the necessary IAM permissions for specific AWS service operations, streamline policy management, and ensure alignment with the latest service updates. The automation of retrieving service reference information eliminates manual effort and allows for seamless integration into policy management tools. This new feature is offered at no additional cost and can be accessed through the documentation on programmatic service reference information","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/aws-service-reference-information-sdk-operation-action-mapping/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"creating-api-gateway-stage","skill_description":"Creates an API Gateway stage with CloudWatch logging, X-Ray tracing, throttling, WAF integration, and IAM roles following AWS best practices. Use when deploying a REST API to different environments such as dev, test, or production.\n\nServices: api-gateway, iam, cloudwatch, wafv2\nTasks: create, configure, secure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: serverless\n*","skill_name":"creating-api-gateway-stage"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"setting-up-ec2-instance-profiles","skill_description":"Configures EC2 instances to securely call AWS services by creating and attaching IAM roles via instance profiles, eliminating hardcoded credentials. Use when an EC2 instance needs permissions to access AWS services like S3, DynamoDB, SQS, or CloudWatch through temporary credentials.\n\nServices: ec2, iam\nTasks: configure, secure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-ec2-instance-profiles"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"AWS Sustainability service now includes water withdrawals data - AWS","context":"AWS Sustainability, a service offered by Amazon Web Services (AWS), has expanded its capabilities to include annual water withdrawals data for workloads. This enhancement enables organizations to obtain a comprehensive understanding of their environmental impact, as it complements the existing carbon emissions data. The water withdrawals data is accessible through the AWS Sustainability console and API, and is available on an annual basis by AWS Region, service, and AWS account. The data represents the total volume of water withdrawn for data center operations, with efficiency improvements reflected as lower withdrawal volumes. The water withdrawals data is provided at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where the service is available. To get started, visit the AWS Sustainability user guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/aws-sustainability-water-withdrawals/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"managing-data-asset-access","skill_description":"Grants, requests, audits and removes access to data assets in an AWS data catalog (the Amazon SageMaker Catalog supported by Amazon DataZone) through catalog subscriptions over published listings. Covers requesting a subscription, approving or rejecting requests with a recorded decision, sharing a listing with a project, revoking one or many subscriptions, and confirming grant settlement. Triggers on: give another team access to a table, request access to a dataset, approve or reject an access request, share a listing with a project, who has access to this table, revoke access, bulk revoke, is the access actually gone, subscription grant status. Not for: IAM roles, policies or STS (use aws-iam), S3 bucket policies (use securing-s3-buckets), Clean Rooms permissions (use aws-cleanrooms), or writing catalog metadata, glossaries and forms, publishing listings, or retiring or deleting an asset that other teams are subscribed to and the order of operations that needs (use managing-data-catalog)\n\n\nServices: datazone\nTasks: deploy, audit\nPersona: data-engineer, developer, architect\nWorkload: data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"managing-data-asset-access"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify IAM permission needed for AWS Sustainability water allocation API."}
